* PATH - DISPLAY OR CHANGE Z-SYSTEM PATH

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* PATH - DISPLAY OR CHANGE Z-SYSTEM PATH

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    A0:PATH
    A0:PATH /C directory-list

With no arguments, displays the current Z-System search path. /C replaces
it; /P prefixes entries; /A appends; /D deletes; /R removes entries from
the end. Changes require wheel privileges.

The supplied startup uses PATH /C A0 so caller command lookup starts in
the public command directory. Do not add private SYSUTLS: to a caller
search path. This changes Z-System lookup, not macOS PATH.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
